{"name":"Craft Juggler","hex":"#e3c8aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"craft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Strength; power; might; force .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}.","Intellectual power; skill; art."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make by hand and with much skill.","To construct, develop something (like a skilled craftsman)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/craft"},{"term":"juggler","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Agent noun of juggle; one who either literally juggles objects, or figuratively juggles tasks.","A person who practices juggling (trick of throwing and catching balls or similar)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Misspelling of jugular."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/juggler"}],"entries":[{"title":"Craft","blocks":[{"text":"A craft or trade is a pastime or an occupation that requires particular skills and knowledge of skilled work. In a historical sense, particularly the Middle Ages and earlier, the term is usually applied to people occupied in small scale production of goods, or their maintenance, for example by tinkers. The traditional term craftsman is nowadays often replaced by artisan and by craftsperson."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Craft_fair_and_folk_festival_Bangladesh_2024_at_Sonargaon_museum_35.jpg/330px-Craft_fair_and_folk_festival_Bangladesh_2024_at_Sonargaon_museum_35.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craft","wikidata":"Q2207288"},{"title":"Juggling","blocks":[{"text":"Juggling is a physical skill, performed by a juggler, involving the manipulation of objects for recreation, entertainment, art, or sport. The most recognizable form of juggling is toss juggling. Juggling can be the manipulation of one object or many objects at the same time, most often using one or two hands but other body parts as well, like feet or head. Jugglers often refer to the objects they juggle as props. The most common props are balls, clubs, or rings. Some jugglers use more dramatic objects such as knives, fire torches or chainsaws. The term juggling can also commonly refer to other prop-based manipulation skills, such as diabolo, plate spinning, devil sticks, poi, cigar boxes, contact juggling, hooping, yo-yo, hat manipulation and kick-ups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Afghan_circus.jpg/330px-Afghan_circus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juggling","wikidata":"Q194326"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg/500px-Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg/1280px-Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg/500px-Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shoes are repaired by a skilled shoemaker; here he evaluates a pair of shoes with a customer watching.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/NSRW_Japanese_potter_at_his_wheel.jpg/500px-NSRW_Japanese_potter_at_his_wheel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/NSRW_Japanese_potter_at_his_wheel.jpg/500px-NSRW_Japanese_potter_at_his_wheel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Japanese potter at his wheel (1914)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANSRW_Japanese_potter_